{"seq":3,"slug":"transportation-distribution","title":"运输与配送","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/management/logistics-mgmt/transportation-distribution","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"transportation-modes","title":"大学物流管理 — 运输方式选择","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/management/logistics-mgmt/transportation-distribution/transportation-modes","wordCount":1451,"readingTime":6},{"seq":2,"slug":"vehicle-routing","title":"大学物流管理 — 车辆路径规划","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/management/logistics-mgmt/transportation-distribution/vehicle-routing","wordCount":1464,"readingTime":6},{"seq":3,"slug":"last-mile-delivery","title":"大学物流管理 — 最后一公里配送","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/management/logistics-mgmt/transportation-distribution/last-mile-delivery","wordCount":1643,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"运输与配送\">运输与配送</h1><p>运输是物流中成本占比最高、最直观的环节——货物的每一次物理移动都在这里发生。本章先比较公路、铁路、水运、航空、管道五种运输方式的特性与适用场景，再深入车辆路径规划这一经典的运筹学问题，最后聚焦电商时代最热门也最烧钱的&quot;最后一公里&quot;配送。</p>\n<p>运输与配送既是科学也是艺术。一条路线规划得好，能省下可观的油费和时间；一套配送网络设计得巧，能让用户体验到&quot;快&quot;的同时企业还不亏钱。本章会让你看到数学优化如何在真实的卡车和快递小哥身上发挥作用。</p>\n"}